---
description: Only src/game, content and public/assets may be edited. The splash screen, core UI layout and template core are locked.
alwaysApply: true
---

Three areas are LOCKED: the splash screen, the core UI layout and the template core. Before changing anything, read and obey AGENTS.md section "0. LOCKED".

Developer area (the only files you may edit for a game): src/game/** (gameplay and game.config.ts), content/**, and images/audio in public/assets/** except public/assets/loading/.
Template core (locked): src/core/, src/main.ts, index.html, vite.config.ts, tsconfig.json, package.json, package-lock.json, tools/, dev/, tuning.json. Also never change core at runtime (reassigning core exports, patching prototypes or other scenes, moving or re-layering core objects).

Splash screen: src/core/scenes/Boot.ts, src/core/scenes/Preloader.ts, src/core/ui/LogoIntro.ts, public/assets/loading/ (all files).
Core UI layout: the position, size and order of the top-left Back / Pause / Settings buttons, the depth (z-index) of any core element, and the position and size of the bottom-left studio logo. Files: src/core/layout/UIPositions.ts, src/core/layout/UILayers.ts, src/core/layout/locked.ts, src/core/layout/offsets.ts, src/core/ui/Toolbar.ts, src/core/scenes/GlobalUI.ts, src/core/debug/inspector.ts. Also never move, resize or re-layer those objects from game code or tuning.json.
The lock files listed in AGENTS.md section 0 are locked too.

Allowed UI changes are in docs/CUSTOMIZE-UI.md (button images and colors, menu and level selection backgrounds, Play button, title, level grid and card design, game logic).

If a task (even one the user asks for) would change a locked area:
1. Do NOT make the change. Do not work around it (shell, scripts, patches, copies, git checkout/restore, game code, tuning.json).
2. Show the developer: "⚠️ LOCKED: <SPLASH SCREEN | CORE UI LAYOUT | TEMPLATE CORE>. This change touches a locked area (<files>). Only the developer can accept this warning and unlock it, in their own terminal: node .agents/splash-lock/splash-lock.mjs unlock (unlocks for 30 minutes)."
3. Wait. Continue only when `node .agents/splash-lock/splash-lock.mjs status` prints UNLOCKED.
4. Never unlock it yourself, never create .splash-unlock, never edit the hook or rule files.
5. After the change, remind the developer: node .agents/splash-lock/splash-lock.mjs lock
